  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e9620f8c34305754d8cc9a7e49e852d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: Ghosts_en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Localization::UnityEngine.Localization.Tables.StringTable
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 59adea3bb3554c548b847491dbd6bc64, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 34469605408768
    m_Localized: WISP
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 37744564109312
    m_Localized: POLTERGEIST
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 37744606052352
    m_Localized: SHADE
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 55670524477440
    m_Localized: A lost flicker of someone who forgot the way home. Harmless, curious
      and easily startled. Every agent's first catch.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 55670549643264
    m_Localized: "Noisy, restless and impatient. When cornered, it vanishes \u2014
      only to reappear a few steps away. Keep your beam steady."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 55670549643265
    m_Localized: It lives between frames. Your lens catches it only in flashes. Patience
      is the only tool that works.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 123991227760640
    m_Localized: WRAITH
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 123991269703680
    m_Localized: It never stops running. The moment your beam touches it, it tears
      sideways out of the ring. Aim where it is going, not where it was.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 123991273897984
    m_Localized: BANSHEE
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 123991273897985
    m_Localized: Her cry shatters the lens. Come too close while she is visible and
      she shrieks, and you lose her. Keep your distance.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 123991273897986
    m_Localized: MIMIC
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 123991273897987
    m_Localized: It lies to your instruments. The EMF points one way while its whisper
      comes from another. Trust your ears until the lens catches it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925186531328
    m_Localized: Night-shift nurses swear a small light drifts down the corridor
      at 3 a.m. and flees from anyone who calls out to it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308544
    m_Localized: Slow and harmless. It drifts around the room at a lazy pace, bolts
      from the beam and calms down again after a couple of seconds.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308545
    m_Localized: 'The moment it notices you, it freezes: that is when to hit the
      beam. Get close, since the beam bites harder up close, and hold on through
      its last struggle.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308546
    m_Localized: 'Agency file 0-01: every wisp analysed so far carries the same faint
      signal, a lullaby hummed at 432 Hz. Nobody knows whose.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308547
    m_Localized: 'It freezes when it notices you: beam it right then, from up close.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308548
    m_Localized: Plates fly off shelves and doors slam in empty rooms. Tenants say
      the cold spot never stays in one place for long.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308549
    m_Localized: "Once the capture passes 40%, it teleports 2\u20133 m away. It needs
      about 5 seconds before it can jump again."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308550
    m_Localized: 'Every jump leaves it dazed for about a second. Sweep the lens,
      lock on fast and beam it while it is stunned: the capture charges twice as
      fast.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308551
    m_Localized: 'Poltergeists are not the spirits of the dead. Agency data suggests
      they feed on stress: every one was found in a home in the middle of a quarrel.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308552
    m_Localized: 'After a teleport it is dazed for a second: lock on at once and
      the beam charges double.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308553
    m_Localized: Drivers on the old bypass see a pale figure at the roadside, and
      swear it was on the other side of the road a heartbeat later.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308554
    m_Localized: The fastest runner on file. Under the beam it dashes 1.5 m sideways
      across your line of sight, every 2 seconds.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308555
    m_Localized: 'Every dash ends with a dead stop for a split second. Don''t chase
      the dash: wait for the stop and hit it then. A wide ring (W2 Floodlight) or
      a tethering beam helps keep it in view.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308556
    m_Localized: Wraiths are echoes of people who died in a hurry. They are not running
      from you; they are still running to whatever they were late for.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308557
    m_Localized: 'After each dash the wraith stops for a split second: strike right
      then.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308558
    m_Localized: It turns up in the corner of old photos and home videos, but never
      twice in the same frame.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308559
    m_Localized: 'Flickers in and out: visible for 1.2 s of every 2 s. The beam only
      charges while it is visible, and progress fades in the gaps.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308560
    m_Localized: 'Its only weak moment is the first: when it notices you, it freezes.
      After that, hold the beam through the gaps without moving the ring. The P4
      Phase Lance keeps its grip even while it is gone.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308561
    m_Localized: 'A shade is not a spirit but a single moment: the frame a camera
      missed. Agency tapes show the same shade in houses 900 km apart, on the same
      night.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308562
    m_Localized: Strike when it first freezes, then keep the ring still through its
      flicker.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308563
    m_Localized: Neighbours hear a woman crying through the walls the night before
      something goes wrong. The ones who went to look don't talk about it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308564
    m_Localized: 'Come closer than about 2.3 m while she is revealed and she shrieks:
      she drops out of the lens for 2 s and the reveal resets. She needs 9 s to shriek
      again.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308565
    m_Localized: 'Keep your distance until she shrieks. She comes back out of the
      static exhausted and won''t shriek again for 9 seconds: that is the moment
      to rush in close and beam her.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308566
    m_Localized: "Every banshee recording in the archive, slowed down 8\xD7, contains
      a name. Never the same one. Agents are advised not to listen to them alone."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308567
    m_Localized: 'After her shriek she comes back exhausted: rush in and beam her
      then.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308568
    m_Localized: It talks in your own voice from the next room. The EMF meters in
      that house never pointed the same way twice.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308569
    m_Localized: 'The EMF lies: it points at a fake source at least 2.5 m away and
      moves it every 5 s. The whisper comes from where it really is. Once revealed,
      the lie stops.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308570
    m_Localized: 'Trust your ears, not the meter: turn towards the whisper, then
      sweep the lens. Once exposed it is stunned for two seconds, your best window.
      It resists hard, so bring spare batteries.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308571
    m_Localized: 'The agency''s first mimic was never caught. Its file still reads
      ''Agent on duty: unknown'', in handwriting that matches every agent who has
      read it.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 350925203308572
    m_Localized: 'Follow the whisper, not the meter. Once revealed it is stunned
      for 2 seconds: strike.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 438211471343616
    m_Localized: Lurker
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 438211513286656
    m_Localized: 'Tall, thin and patient. It never comes at you head-on: it waits
      until you look away and closes in one silent step at a time.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 438211513286657
    m_Localized: Night guards all report the same figure at the end of the corridor,
      a little closer every time they look back at the monitor. Nobody has seen it
      before eleven.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 438211513286658
    m_Localized: 'Moves only while you look away: the moment the camera turns to
      it, it freezes. It creeps up behind you and edges closer; let it reach your
      back and it lunges. It only comes out between 23:00 and 04:00.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 438211513286659
    m_Localized: 'Listen to the floor: a creak means it has set off again. Turn round
      at once and you catch it mid-step, winded for a moment. Keep it in view while
      you beam it: watched, it cannot run.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 438211513286660
    m_Localized: 'Every lurker file ends the same way: the agent''s last recording
      is a shot of their own back, taken from just above head height.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 438211513286661
    m_Localized: 'The Lurker only moves when you look away: when the floor creaks,
      turn round at once.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 438211513286662
    m_Localized: Phantom Cat
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 438211513286663
    m_Localized: A small, curious spirit that still thinks it lives here. It hates
      sudden moves and loves a quiet lap.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 438211513286664
    m_Localized: Tenants hear purring from an empty armchair and find a warm dent
      at the foot of the bed in the morning. Nobody in the building keeps a cat.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 438211513286665
    m_Localized: A sudden step or a quick turn of the camera sends it running for
      a couple of seconds. Stand still for a moment and it comes over and sits about
      1.2 m away. It never scares anyone; it meows.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 438211513286666
    m_Localized: 'Freeze and let it come to you. While it sits and purrs it is wide
      open for up to 3 seconds: beam it without moving the phone.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 438211513286667
    m_Localized: Phantom cats are not the ghosts of pets. They are what a home remembers
      of the evenings it was happy.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 438211513286668
    m_Localized: 'The cat runs from sudden moves: stand still and let it come and
      sit by you.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
